Subject: PowerShell SHA256 HashData Compatibility Fault

& [OperationalFault] is closed
  + [fault_uuid] is 56f69a07-b5ad-4c3b-aa3a-2e39e793012e
  + [observed_at_time_ms] is 1785958240001
  + [operation] is compute an in-memory aggregate digest over the changed current-manifest set
  + [expected] is one lowercase SHA-256 digest without a temporary file
  + [observed] is the host .NET runtime did not expose the static SHA256.HashData API
  + [effect] is the first aggregate digest field was empty; prior frozen-hash and allowed-key checks had already passed and no repository content changed
  + [resolution] is use SHA256.Create().ComputeHash over the same in-memory UTF-8 payload
  + [result] is aggregate SHA256 8ca4d090bf6b6baf6d90c1b8a5af88e1b0e4975e75e9b14098f5b2489d609538
  + [prevention] is prefer the compatible instance ComputeHash API in Windows PowerShell 5.1 orchestration
